# Batch 11 — extraction uncertainties (UNC) and human adjudication queue (HQ). Written after extraction of Articles 1–99.
unc("A4.P0;A57.P1;A58.P1;A58.P2;A58.P3;A70.P1;A83.P4;A83.P5", "coding-rule", "Granularity: 382 point-level units were inventoried automatically, but screening and extraction were done at paragraph level. Long lists (Art.4 definitions; Art.57(1) 22 tasks; Art.58 powers; Art.70(1) 25 tasks; Art.83(4)-(5) tiers) were grouped into few records, with point citations only where relation-bearing points were separated or linked.", "Point-level distinctions (e.g. which of the 22 SA tasks is a relation and which a self-contained duty) may be lost; extraction coverage is therefore 'paragraph-level complete, point-level partial'.")
unc("A57.P1.ptf;A77.P1;A77.P2;A60.P7", "coding-rule", "Possible duplicate observations: the complaint-handling duty of the SA appears in QR for Art.57(1)(f) (with Art.77 units linked), Art.77(2) and Art.60(7). They were kept as distinct statements by unit but state overlapping duties.", "Counts of relations in SC-10 and SC-07 may overstate independent observations; many-to-many provenance (not duplication) is the intended rule.")
unc("A12.P4;A77.P2;A57.P1.ptf", "interpretation", "Relation type 'information/reporting' is used for 106 of 238 relations (44.5%) and lumps notifications, consultations, cooperation, reasons-giving and information duties. V6's ten relation types do not provide a type for peer cooperation, jurisdictional or liability allocation.", "Type-level analyses (e.g. 'information relations dominate') are artefacts of the type inventory; discrimination is carried by `function`, `object` and `type_note`.")
unc("A5.P2;A24.P1;A58.P1;A58.P2;A83.P2", "inference", "Accountability is recorded unit by unit (INFO / ANSWERABILITY candidates). A **derived** controller/processor→SA accountability relation can be assembled across Arts 5(2), 24(1), 58(1)(a),(e), 58(2), 83 (see INITIAL_ARCHITECTURAL_PROFILE §5) but was not entered as an extraction record because it is a reconstruction, not a provision-level observation.", "AC (full) appears only as a derived, cross-provision relation; no single unit satisfies all five elements.")
unc("A21.P5", "coding-rule", "Unit left on Hold: a permission of the data subject to object by automated means without an identifiable counterpart in the unit; referred to Directive 2002/58/EC.", "No record; unit counted as screened with extraction status Hold.")
unc("A1.P3;A2.P3;A4.P0.pt7;A6.P3;A10.P0;A23.P1;A49.P5;A53.P4;A85.P1;A89.P2", "interpretation", "Twenty assignments have an unstated or unnamed subject ('Union or Member State law', passive voice, unspecified legislator). They are recorded as NA with `subject-unstated`; no actor was invented.", "These provisions describe the rule-making competence of national and Union legislators, which is not represented as a position of the architecture.")
unc("A4.P0.pt7;A4.P0.pt8;A4.P0.pt22;A56.P1", "ontology", "Functionally defined positions: controller, processor, joint controllers, supervisory authority concerned and lead supervisory authority are roles defined by conduct or by facts (determining purposes and means; establishment; affected data subjects), not legally specified offices. They were recorded as `position_type` with a note.", "The ontology's notion of 'a legally specified place' does not fit them straightforwardly (TP-01).")
unc("A43.P1;A53.P1;A54.P1;A68.P3;A93.P1", "external dependency", "Several decisive constitutive dependencies lie outside W and were not retrieved: Member State law constituting each SA (EXT-015); Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 and EN-ISO/IEC 17065/2012 (EXT-009–011); the instrument constituting the EDPS (EXT-017); Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 (EXT-008, 018, 019).", "Absence-dependent claims and some S→A outcomes are limited to W or indeterminate.")
unc("A6.P1;A9.P2;A14.P5;A17.P3;A23.P1;A49.P1;A85.P2;A88.P1;A89.P2;A90.P1", "external dependency", "Generic references to 'Union or Member State law' occur throughout (29 records carry an explicit Member State law dependency; 48 records mention Union or Member State law). Only constitutive references were registered as EXT rows (22 rows for roughly 16 distinct sources, with some sources repeated per provision); generic national-law references are not in the external-reference register.", "The external-reference register is incomplete for generic national-law dependencies; counts of external dependencies are lower bounds.")
unc("A99.P1;A99.P2;A92.P2;A51.P4;A83.P9", "coding-rule", "All records carry the baseline `legal_status_of_norm` (in force; applicable from 25 May 2018). Provision-level dates (24 May 2016; 25 May 2018; 25 May 2020) are mentioned in notes but are not coded unit by unit.", "Legal status is not time-indexed at unit level.")
unc("(all recitals)", "coding-rule", "Recitals were extracted into the working text but not reviewed for interpretive context beyond their identification as non-operative. No record was created from a recital.", "Interpretive ambiguities (e.g. 62(7)) are unresolved; a recital review is a pending step.")
unc("A1.P1;A2.P1;A3.P1", "coding-rule", "Sixty units (15%) were screened 'No' as scope, exceptions, content specifications or passive substantive rules. Several (e.g. exceptions in 14(5), 17(3), 22(2)) modify the conditions of recorded relations but were not coded as separate records.", "Condition fields of the affected relations are summarised in their notes.")

hq("Do procedures (cooperation under Art.60, mutual assistance, joint operations, the consistency mechanism, the urgency procedure) meet the DEV threshold (identity + operator/rules/bounded function), and are they devices at all?", "Ten PD records are flagged DEV-threshold. Treating procedures as devices inflates the device category; treating them as relations loses their identity as a legally set-out procedure with its own rules.", "(a) procedures as DEV; (b) procedures as sets of relations (INS-TYPE); (c) a separate 'procedure' kind", "No")
hq("Is an 'obligation to designate/appoint an office-holder' (DPO, representative, joint representative) an N2 or a separate norm type?", "The Regulation specifies the office at type level; the instance arises from a private act. N1–N4 do not state who constitutes the instance.", "(a) N2-designation as used here; (b) new norm type; (c) record only the duty", "No")
hq("Does the 'mediated constitution' of the national supervisory authorities (Union obligation in Arts 51(1)/54(1)(a) → establishment by Member State law) count as 'legally constituted' within W?", "The formal architecture of the GDPR contains the obligation and the competence, not the authorities. V6's 'legally constituted configuration' must say by which legal order.", "(a) only the obligation is constituted within W; (b) a two-step category of mediated constitution; (c) widen W to national law", "Yes (conceptual)")
hq("From what date does the N1 establishment of the Board (Art.68(1)) take effect — entry into force (24 May 2016) or application (25 May 2018)?", "Determines the temporal reference of the 'legal constitution evidenced' claim for the Board; Art.92(2) shows provisions with effect from entry into force.", "(a) 25 May 2018; (b) 24 May 2016; (c) not determinable from W", "No")
hq("Is a derived controller/processor→SA relation satisfying all five accountability elements across several provisions (5(2), 24(1), 58(1)(a),(e), 58(2), 83) admissible as ACCOUNTABILITY under DR-10?", "It is the only candidate for full AC in W; the 'questioning' capacity rests on 58(1)(a),(e). The classification depends on how strictly derivation across provisions is allowed.", "(a) admit as derived; (b) require a single provision; (c) require explicit questioning capacity", "No")
hq("Should 'questioning capacity' be required explicitly? (Board→SA after 64(8); courts→SA; legislature→Commission).", "Without it the relations stay ANSWERABILITY or INFO although assessment and consequences exist. The requirement may be too strict for institutions whose procedures are set outside W.", "(a) keep as is; (b) accept institutionally implied questioning where a binding review decision exists", "Yes")
hq("Do V6's ten relation types suffice? Peer cooperation, liability allocation, jurisdiction rules and court-to-court coordination had no type; 106 of 238 relations are 'information/reporting'.", "Type inflation hides differences relevant to S→A (consultation, escalation, standstill).", "(a) keep and rely on `function` and `type_note`; (b) add secondary subtypes; (c) propose an additional type to David", "Yes")
hq("Independent re-discovery of subconfigurations: the S predicates were written by the same agent after extraction.", "Candidate S may encode the analyst's expectations; false positives were found in SC-10.", "A second coder defines S blind to these; compare; or use a documented clustering method as a comparator", "Yes (before any publication use)")
hq("Competing S→A hypotheses with consequential outcomes: AI-03 (conditional integration), AI-04 (shared interfaces vs one assurance architecture), AI-05 (indeterminate), AI-07 (mediated constitution), AI-08 (W=A not supported).", "These are the pilot's substantive claims.", "Independent legal review and blind recoding of coupling (I2) for each AI record", "Yes")
hq("Retrieve and read Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 (committee procedure) and the instrument constituting the EDPS before any claim on Commission rule-making control (AI-05) or on the Board's membership.", "Decisive external dependencies for AI-05 and AI-07.", "Targeted retrieval of the cited Articles only (no automatic corpus expansion)", "No")
hq("Art.62(7): referent of 'its Member State' ('may adopt a provisional measure on the territory of its Member State').", "Direction of the peer-enforcement relation.", "Specialist legal reading; recital and case-law check", "No")
hq("Is 'Union or Member State law' (an unnamed legislator) a position, an origin of competence, or neither?", "20 NA records have unstated subjects; the architecture of rule-making competence is partly represented through them.", "Treat as source of norms (not a position); record competence only", "No")
hq("Does optionality of enhancement (codes 'may'; certification 'voluntary') defeat the V6 'institutionalized enhancement' condition for enhanced self-regulation (AI-09)?", "Determines whether the pattern is a property of the instrument or only of adherents.", "(a) conditional layer (as recorded); (b) condition not met", "Yes")
hq("Later amendments to the GDPR and later official corrigenda after 3 October 2026 were not verified.", "The baseline is a historical authentic text with the 2018 corrigendum; it must not be described as the currently applicable GDPR. The 2021 corrigendum (CELEX 32016R0679R(03)) was not retrievable in English.", "Check EUR-Lex amendment/corrigendum records at the time of any publication", "No")
hq("Treatment of Art.85(2), 90 and 23: national law may derogate from provisions that constitute the architecture itself (Chapters VI–VII).", "A boundary issue not covered by I4 as formulated: the instrument's own scope is conditional on national derogations.", "Add a boundary note to every AI record; or a 'self-modifying scope' flag", "Yes")
hq("Art.21(5) left on Hold.", "Permission without identifiable counterpart; refers to Directive 2002/58/EC.", "Legal reading", "No")
